F-0266 sweep — how many gates could not tell code from a comment
dev, 2026-08-18, task T-BRANDOPEN-0817

METHOD. Reading 122 gates and judging them would produce an opinion. Instead each
gate was run three times against the same source tree and its EXIT CODE compared:

  BASELINE   a pristine copy of src/ + influora-api/src (+ configs), 17MB, 1612 files
  MUTANT A   the same tree, except every source file a gate reads has that gate's
             OWN TEXT appended to it as a `//` comment block. This is the F-0266
             shape made mechanical: "the fix documented itself, quoting the rule".
             A gate whose verdict changes has read a comment as code.
  MUTANT B   the same tree with ALL comments removed from every .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/
             .java file. A gate whose verdict changes was RELYING on comment text
             to pass — the mirror disease, a false GREEN.

A HARNESS BUG WORTH RECORDING, because the first run of this sweep was wrong.
44 of the 97 shell gates resolve their project root as
`ROOT=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../..")` and IGNORE the project-dir argument entirely.
Run from .proof-os/gates they read the REAL repo no matter what tree you hand them,
so the first sweep silently measured the unmutated repo for those 44 and reported
5 affected gates. Fixed by copying the gates dir INTO each sweep tree
(<tree>/.proof-os/gates/) so both root conventions land on the tree under test.
The corrected sweep found 12. Anyone re-running this must do the same, and it is
its own small finding: those 44 gates cannot be pointed at a worktree.

STATIC PASS (all 122 files under .proof-os/gates/)
  122  gate files scanned          (97 .sh, 25 .py/.mjs)
   51  grep source text and did NOT strip comments   -> structurally exposed
    1  already stripped comments (F-0238, partially — see below)
   37  name a source path but never grep it (they run vitest instead)
   36  touch no source path at all (npm audit, gitleaks, eslint, doc checks)

EMPIRICAL PASS (the 52 gates that grep source text, corrected harness)
  MUTANT A — verdict changed by a COMMENT: 12 gates
      F-0235-no-fabricated-pii-live.sh              0 -> 1
      F-0239-no-fake-money-progress.sh              0 -> 1
      F-0241-no-false-draft-reassurance.sh          0 -> 1
      F-0242-brand-can-open-dispute.sh              0 -> 1
      F-0243-verification-copy-agrees.sh            0 -> 1
      F-0247-premature-success-copy.sh              2 -> 1
      F-0248-unreachable-primary-action.sh          2 -> 1
      F-0253-signature-canvas-submitted.sh          2 -> 1
      F-0256-no-mock-campaign-seed.sh               2 -> 1
      F-0258-no-client-invented-fees.sh             2 -> 1
      F-0265-brand-palette-tokens.sh                0 -> 1
      F-0294-server-fee-copy-rendered.sh            2 -> 1
    plus F-0238 itself, reproduced separately at exit 1 (F-0266.prefix.log).

  MUTANT B — verdict changed by REMOVING comments: 0 gates
    No gate in this tree currently passes because of comment text. The false-GREEN
    direction is possible (F-0224 below is the shape) but not presently realised.

  12 is a LOWER BOUND, not a census. Mutant A can only fire when a gate's pattern
  survives being pasted into a comment; a pattern written as an escaped ERE
  (`@Column\(name = "terms_text"\)`) does not match its own source text, so a gate
  can be fully exposed and show no flip. That is why the fix was applied to the
  structural population (51), not only to the 12 that happened to trigger.

WHAT WAS FIXED
  gates/_strip_comments.py  pre-existing tokenizer, kept. One REAL BUG found and
        fixed while wiring it up: it wrote its output with `sys.stdout.write`,
        which on this Windows host encodes cp1252, so every source file containing
        `₹` (the money screens) or `→` (the admin audit panels) crashed it with
        UnicodeEncodeError and the calling gate reported UNAVAILABLE. Honest, but
        it silently excluded the money surfaces from comment-aware checking. Now
        writes UTF-8 bytes to sys.stdout.buffer.
  gates/_code.sh            NEW shared helper, the house `_rc.sh` convention.
        code_ready / code_view / code_of / code_grep_r / code_why.
        code_view returns a PATH to a comment-blanked copy with newlines preserved,
        so it is a drop-in for "$F" in grep/sed/awk AND `grep -n` still reports the
        original line numbers. If the stripper cannot run it reports UNAVAILABLE
        and never falls back to grepping raw bytes — a silent fallback would restore
        the defect invisibly.

  50 gates now source it:
     48 by mechanical patch (SELF before the cd, source + code_ready after it,
        VAR_CODE=$(code_view "$VAR"), and "$VAR" -> "$VAR_CODE" ONLY on lines whose
        command is grep/sed/awk/wc/head/tail/nl — never in prose or NOT-CHECKED text)
      1 F-0238 migrated off its private inline stripper onto the shared one
      1 F-0050 hand-patched: it carried the SAME naive `^\s*(//|\*|\{/\*)` filter
        that F-0238 had, applied to only one of its three checks
      1 F-0224 hand-patched: `grep -rn "releasePayout" src/` over a whole directory,
        REQUIRING a hit. One comment anywhere under src/ saying "the releasePayout
        call was removed here" proved the escrow-release endpoint still had a way
        out of the product. A false green over money movement. Now code_grep_r,
        which pre-filters with a raw grep (correctness is unaffected — a raw grep can
        only over-select) and tokenizes only the candidates: 200s+ -> 11.5s.

  NOT AFFECTED, checked and dismissed with a reason:
     F-0207 greps package.json — JSON has no comments.
     brand_pipeline_static_components.sh, fund_escrow_onfunded.sh — they grep the
     OUTPUT of eslint / vitest, not source text.

PROOF, both directions
  F-0238, hardened, run against three trees:
      comment-only occurrence (correct tree)  exit 0   (was 1)
      real reintroduction IN CODE             exit 1   (still catches it)
      the real repo                           exit 0
  Whole population, corrected harness, after the fix:
      BASELINE vs BASELINE-after-patch : 0 verdicts changed out of 52
      BASELINE-after-patch vs MUTANT A : 0 flips remaining (was 12)

WHAT THIS SWEEP STILL CANNOT SEE
  - Template literals and regex literals containing `/` are tokenized loosely
    (documented in _strip_comments.py). A forbidden string inside a `${...}`
    interpolation that itself contains a string may be mis-scoped.
  - A string that is real code but DEAD code still counts as present. The helper
    tells comment from code, not reachable from unreachable.
  - The 37 gates that run vitest instead of grepping are untouched by this and are
    a different trust question entirely.
  - Mutant A under-detects (see above). 12 is what fired, 51 is what is exposed.

================================================================================
ADDENDUM — what the mechanical pass missed, found by auditing its own output
================================================================================
The 48-gate mechanical patch swaps "$VAR" -> "$VAR_CODE" on reader lines. It cannot
see a read that goes through a LOOP variable. Scanning the patched gates for
`for x in "$A" "$B"; do ... grep "$x"` found 7 loops, of which 5 are harmless
existence checks (`[ -f "$f" ]`) and 2 were real residual raw reads:

  F-0243-verification-copy-agrees.sh:32   for f in "$K" "$B"; grep -qE "...publishes? automatically" "$f"
  F-0273-frozen-escrow-reads-frozen.sh:43 for enum_file in "$ENUM_MS" "$ENUM_ES"; grep -q "$s" "$enum_file"

Both hand-fixed. This is worth recording as its own hazard: a PARTIALLY converted
gate is worse than an unconverted one, because it now carries the F-0266 preamble
and reads as hardened. Any future mechanical pass over these gates must audit its
own output for loop-variable reads, not just count swaps.

FALSE-GREEN CONTROL (the mirror disease, proved on a converted gate)
  F-0243 requires the copy "required to publish" to exist in brand-kyc-prompt.tsx.
      clean tree                                             exit 0
      copy deleted from CODE                                 exit 1
      copy deleted from CODE, restated in a COMMENT          exit 1   <- the point
      restored                                               exit 0
  Before the fix the third row would have been exit 0: a gate certifying copy that
  had been deleted, because someone described it in a comment.

FALSE-RED CONTROL (a converted gate still catches real code)
  F-0235 forbids a fabricated address in live component state.
      clean tree                                             exit 0
      `useState("Sea View, Carter Road")` added as CODE      exit 1
      the same text added as a `//` comment                  exit 0
